{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789040655,"nonce":"k/CxaSS8OYlUZLXwcjahw1JgJiY=","title":"The wasm arms error on all eleven sqlite sys tests","message":"sys under ash:wasm and ash:wasm-fibers is 1101/1112 assertions with **11 errors** and 0 failures, while ash:interp and ash:aot both pass 1118/1118 and stock hashlink passes too. Errors, not failures, so these are thrown exceptions rather than wrong answers; the denominator drops to 1112 because an error abandons the rest of its test.\n\nBoth wasm arms fail identically, which puts it in the sqlite side module or its binding rather than in the fiber transform.\n\nNamed in the run detail: testDbName, testIssue9700, testLastInsertId, testTransactionCommit, testTransactionRollback, testAsIterator, and five more.\n\n**Ruled out already: missing primitives.** `ash wasm target/release/wasm32-wasip1/hdll/sqlite.wasm` lists all eleven the native hdll defines --- hlp_connect, hlp_close, hlp_request, hlp_last_id, hlp_result_get, hlp_result_get_fields, hlp_result_get_float, hlp_result_get_int, hlp_result_get_length, hlp_result_get_nfields, hlp_result_next. The module is valid, 1968 functions, and its 39 unsatisfied env imports are the ordinary side-module set (memory, __stack_pointer, malloc, free) that the main module supplies through dylink. Do not spend a second pass on export coverage.\n\nNote for whoever picks this up: `strings` on a wasm module answers MISSING for symbols that are present. It did so for all eleven of these and for hlp_hash_gen earlier the same day. Use `ash wasm \u003cmodule\u003e`.\n\n**Not reproducible on macOS.** A local sys sweep gives 984/984 on all four engines with zero errors. The local build CONTAINS the sqlite cases -- testDbName and testLastInsertId are in the compiled sys.hl -- but they never execute, and the local suite runs 134 assertions fewer than CI does. So the reproduction needs Linux with the suite CI builds: the NUC or a CI run.","files":null}]}